WEBVTT

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.865
Spectacular, isn't it?

00:00:47.866 --> 00:00:49.533
Probably! What is it?

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:51.368
I've created a simulation

00:00:51.369 --> 00:00:53.495
of the entire universe!

00:00:55.198 --> 00:00:57.866
Oh! In that case, it stinks.

00:00:57.867 --> 00:00:59.868
I keep forgetting, Professor.

00:00:59.869 --> 00:01:01.829
Are we in the entire universe?

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.163
Why, naturally!

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.250
Good news, everyone!

00:01:06.251 --> 00:01:07.876
We've got a delivery!

00:01:09.921 --> 00:01:12.339
But first, roll call!

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.841
Leela? 3-PIXEL LEELA: Here.

00:01:13.842 --> 00:01:15.510
- Fry?
- Present!

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.761
- Scruffy?
- Yep.

00:01:17.762 --> 00:01:19.431
- Hermes?
- Check.

00:01:19.431 --> 00:01:20.431
Bender?

00:01:20.432 --> 00:01:22.391
Bite
my shiny middle pixel!

00:01:22.392 --> 00:01:24.685
- Amy?
- Shmobviously.

00:01:24.686 --> 00:01:26.020
And the rest.

00:01:26.021 --> 00:01:29.273
Hooray! I'm
an unnamed member of the group!

00:01:29.274 --> 00:01:31.317
That's amazing, Professor!

00:01:31.318 --> 00:01:32.943
How'd you make it so crummy?

00:01:32.944 --> 00:01:36.447
It wasn't easy. Even to
achieve this level of realism

00:01:36.448 --> 00:01:39.450
requires vast amounts
of computing power.

00:01:40.452 --> 00:01:43.454
My Simputron uses
more electricity

00:01:43.455 --> 00:01:45.331
than 100 bug zappers.

00:01:45.332 --> 00:01:49.043
Which reminds me, I had
to unplug our bug zappers.

00:01:52.839 --> 00:01:54.381
- Ow!
- Got him!

00:01:54.382 --> 00:01:56.550
The mosquito is still alive.

00:01:56.551 --> 00:01:57.968
There's a mosquito?

00:02:00.305 --> 00:02:01.722
Listen up, threeple!

00:02:01.723 --> 00:02:05.392
Today, you'll be delivering
this package to Space Italy.

00:02:05.393 --> 00:02:06.977
Space Italy?

00:02:06.978 --> 00:02:10.356
I know, it's an
embarrassingly lazy name.

00:02:10.357 --> 00:02:13.567
But when you're creating an
entire universe from scratch,

00:02:13.568 --> 00:02:16.737
you can't make up a believable
name for everything.

00:02:16.738 --> 00:02:19.990
Sometimes, you just have
to go with "Space Italy"

00:02:19.991 --> 00:02:21.867
or "the Robot Planet"

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:23.702
or "Dr. Zoidberg."

00:02:23.703 --> 00:02:24.912
Preposterous.

00:02:33.371 --> 00:02:35.372
Wow, Space Italy!

00:02:35.373 --> 00:02:37.458
You delivering that
package, Bender?

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:40.461
Up all
those steps? No grazie.

00:02:40.462 --> 00:02:42.963
I'll just chuck it into
Trevi Fountain for good luck.

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.468
Ooh!

00:02:47.469 --> 00:02:50.596
Papa pia!
He hit-a the Space Pope!

00:02:54.142 --> 00:02:57.227
You're under
arrest for-a bonking His Holiness.

00:02:57.228 --> 00:02:59.856
I tell-a
you, this-a Planet Express company

00:02:59.856 --> 00:03:02.066
is a real two-bit operation, eh?

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:04.485
More
like three!

00:03:07.113 --> 00:03:09.990
So, um,
as long as we're here,

00:03:09.991 --> 00:03:11.325
wanna see the sights?

00:03:11.326 --> 00:03:12.910
When
in Space Rome...

00:03:19.125 --> 00:03:22.628
Michelangelo's
David! So lifelike!

00:03:22.629 --> 00:03:24.922
Jeez,
Dave! Get a fig leaf!

00:03:26.174 --> 00:03:27.967
3-PIXEL GONDOLIER
  La la la!

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.593
La la la!

00:03:29.594 --> 00:03:31.136
La la la...

00:03:35.558 --> 00:03:37.936
I just can't
understand how it doesn't fall dow...

00:03:39.521 --> 00:03:40.855
Let me
give you a han...

00:03:47.654 --> 00:03:51.031
Oh, mama, they're goin' at
it like two packs of gum!

00:03:51.032 --> 00:03:53.492
Bender, give us
a little privacy.

00:03:53.493 --> 00:03:55.661
Aw...

00:03:55.662 --> 00:03:57.788
So, do those people
in the casserole

00:03:57.789 --> 00:03:59.790
know they're in a simulation,

00:03:59.791 --> 00:04:01.542
or do they think
that they're real?

00:04:01.543 --> 00:04:03.460
Of course, they
think they're real.

00:04:03.461 --> 00:04:05.629
To them, the rules
of my software

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.840
are just their laws of physics.

00:04:07.841 --> 00:04:10.092
But, we think we're real.

00:04:10.093 --> 00:04:13.137
Couldn't our universe
also be a simulation?

00:04:13.138 --> 00:04:16.307
Absolutely
not! No chance.

00:04:16.308 --> 00:04:19.602
The very idea is preposterous!
- How can you be so sure?

00:04:19.603 --> 00:04:22.396
Because it's
computationally impossible!

00:04:22.397 --> 00:04:25.107
For example, every
atom in the universe

00:04:25.108 --> 00:04:28.277
is affected whenever
one little thing moves.

00:04:28.278 --> 00:04:31.238
Like my ass?

00:04:32.657 --> 00:04:35.075
Oh yeah! Come on!

00:04:35.076 --> 00:04:37.411
That's a
perfect example, Bender,

00:04:37.412 --> 00:04:39.496
and some pretty decent
twerking.

00:04:39.497 --> 00:04:43.250
My software can't possibly
compute the gravitational changes

00:04:43.251 --> 00:04:46.170
between Bender's ass and
every other particle,

00:04:46.171 --> 00:04:49.923
so I had to have the information
travel outward gradually,

00:04:49.924 --> 00:04:51.508
at a fixed speed.

00:04:51.509 --> 00:04:54.011
Like the speed of
light in our universe?

00:04:54.012 --> 00:04:55.387
Right!

00:04:56.723 --> 00:04:59.475
Oh, fuff. That's
just a coincidence.

00:04:59.476 --> 00:05:01.352
I had to cut other corners, too.

00:05:01.353 --> 00:05:03.938
I mean, my simulation
doesn't even keep track

00:05:03.939 --> 00:05:06.482
of exactly where everything is.

00:05:06.483 --> 00:05:07.900
Takin' all bets!

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:10.403
Find the ball, win
me not punching you!

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.031
My last $5
on cup number one!

00:05:14.032 --> 00:05:16.825
In fact, make it my last $10!

00:05:16.826 --> 00:05:19.286
Another convenient example.

00:05:19.287 --> 00:05:23.123
My lazy software wouldn't even
decide which cup the ball's in

00:05:23.124 --> 00:05:25.542
until someone actually looked
at it.

00:05:25.543 --> 00:05:28.922
Until then, it's
just sort of in both.

00:05:32.008 --> 00:05:33.676
So your programming shortcut

00:05:33.677 --> 00:05:35.970
is like quantum
mechanics in our world?

00:05:35.971 --> 00:05:37.846
Exactly like that!

00:05:39.391 --> 00:05:41.225
Hm, interesting.

00:05:41.226 --> 00:05:43.727
I guess what I'm
trying to say is

00:05:43.728 --> 00:05:47.147
our universe is probably
also a simulation.

00:05:48.483 --> 00:05:51.652
But that's the exact opposite
of what you said one minute ago!

00:05:51.653 --> 00:05:55.447
New evidence was presented
and I changed my mind.

00:05:55.448 --> 00:05:57.032
I'm a scientist, not a...

00:05:57.033 --> 00:05:58.492
- Idiot?
- Politician.

00:05:58.493 --> 00:06:00.953
Man. Imagine how
awful it would be

00:06:00.954 --> 00:06:04.373
to find out your whole
personality was just simulated,

00:06:04.374 --> 00:06:05.582
like Bender's.

00:06:05.583 --> 00:06:07.876
Whuzzulated? Like whozer's?

00:06:07.877 --> 00:06:10.754
I just mean you're an
artificial intelligence, Bender.

00:06:10.755 --> 00:06:13.132
Like the people in the
Professor's simulation.

00:06:13.133 --> 00:06:15.634
- Artificial?
- Uh-huh. Yep.

00:06:15.635 --> 00:06:19.179
Why'd you have to tell me?
You just ruined my life!

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.600
My big fat fake life!

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:24.518
You're a walking bucket!

00:06:24.519 --> 00:06:26.729
How can you say I'm not real?!

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.273
If you prick me, do I not bleed?

00:06:32.402 --> 00:06:34.737
Okay, that was a bad example!

00:06:34.738 --> 00:06:36.488
Ow! I'm bleeding!

00:06:36.489 --> 00:06:39.074
- Showoff.
- There, there, Bender.

00:06:39.075 --> 00:06:41.160
You're as real as any of us.

00:06:41.161 --> 00:06:43.370
The philosopher
René Descartes said,

00:06:43.371 --> 00:06:45.497
"I think, therefore I am."

00:06:45.498 --> 00:06:47.750
Can you think?
- I don't think so!

00:06:47.751 --> 00:06:50.085
I think I might not
be able to think!

00:06:50.086 --> 00:06:52.796
Anyway, it was a
fun little universe,

00:06:52.797 --> 00:06:56.300
but we're looking at a
Godzilla-sized electric bill.

00:06:56.301 --> 00:06:58.385
It's time to shut it down.

00:06:58.386 --> 00:07:00.471
But, you can't
just turn them off!

00:07:00.472 --> 00:07:02.348
That would be like
turning me off!

00:07:02.349 --> 00:07:05.684
Good idea! That'll
save even more power!

00:07:05.685 --> 00:07:07.603
But we'll start with them.

00:07:07.604 --> 00:07:08.265
No...

00:07:13.944 --> 00:07:16.445
No...

00:07:17.948 --> 00:07:19.531
The plug is stuck.

00:07:19.532 --> 00:07:22.368
Or maybe
I'm just extraordinarily weak.

00:07:22.369 --> 00:07:24.328
That is a possibility.

00:07:24.329 --> 00:07:28.248
Oh, bother. I'll just keep the
simulation running a little longer.

00:07:28.249 --> 00:07:30.584
Thanks,
Professor!

00:07:30.585 --> 00:07:34.505
Bender, how were you leaping
through the air that entire time?

00:07:34.506 --> 00:07:37.341
I wasn't! My first
leap missed by a mile,

00:07:37.342 --> 00:07:38.717
so I leapt again.

00:07:38.718 --> 00:07:41.679
But I never stopped
screaming for a second!

00:07:44.182 --> 00:07:47.268
I feel like I've been
in existence for a while now, Leela.

00:07:47.269 --> 00:07:50.271
So it's time I set
myself a life's goal.

00:07:50.272 --> 00:07:53.399
That's a great idea!
I'll be quiet and let you think.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:57.278
And I'll turn on the
TV to drown out any distracting noises.

00:08:00.865 --> 00:08:03.993
That's it!
I found my life's goal!

00:08:03.994 --> 00:08:06.996
I, Philip J. Fry, hereby pledge

00:08:06.997 --> 00:08:10.499
to watch every TV
show ever made.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.126
Oh Lord.

00:08:12.127 --> 00:08:14.169
That orange guy sure is dumb.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:17.756
These innocent bit
bags may be artificial,

00:08:17.757 --> 00:08:19.717
like me,

00:08:19.718 --> 00:08:21.218
but they don't know that!

00:08:21.219 --> 00:08:24.555
They deserve the same respect
as any other living creature.

00:08:24.556 --> 00:08:25.723
Except clams!

00:08:25.724 --> 00:08:27.182
To hell with clams!

00:08:27.183 --> 00:08:30.394
I'm telling you they're
nothing but ones and zeros!

00:08:30.395 --> 00:08:31.729
They're no more alive

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:34.690
than the number 10101.

00:08:34.691 --> 00:08:36.233
She was my aunt!

00:08:36.234 --> 00:08:38.902
Professor, I think
Bender might be right.

00:08:38.903 --> 00:08:40.154
No, you don't!

00:08:40.155 --> 00:08:42.990
I mean, we're nothing
more than atoms, right?

00:08:42.991 --> 00:08:45.618
But, somehow, we are more.

00:08:48.913 --> 00:08:50.539
Unlike clams!

00:08:53.418 --> 00:08:57.130
Professor, I will now ask
of you a solemn promise.

00:08:59.841 --> 00:09:01.884
Now, the feet.
- Forget the feet!

00:09:01.885 --> 00:09:03.135
Alright, whatever.

00:09:03.136 --> 00:09:05.137
Why are we in a
robot strip club?

00:09:06.723 --> 00:09:08.933
Because we had to
do this in a place

00:09:08.934 --> 00:09:10.726
that's meaningful to me!

00:09:10.727 --> 00:09:11.770
Bender!

00:09:12.562 --> 00:09:13.854
Here you go, hun.

00:09:13.855 --> 00:09:16.191
- Keep the change, toots.
- Ow!

00:09:20.403 --> 00:09:23.239
Let the solemn ceremony begin.

00:09:23.823 --> 00:09:27.743
Professor, you created a world
of conscious living beings,

00:09:27.744 --> 00:09:30.120
so now you're
responsible for them.

00:09:30.121 --> 00:09:32.915
I want you to swear you'll
do everything in your power

00:09:32.916 --> 00:09:34.333
to keep them alive.

00:09:34.334 --> 00:09:37.503
I barely make any effort
to keep myself alive.

00:09:37.504 --> 00:09:38.629
Oof!
- Professor!

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:41.632
And you'll never let them
know they're not real! Never!

00:09:41.633 --> 00:09:44.093
So they won't have to go
through what I'm going through!

00:09:44.094 --> 00:09:46.220
I swear nothing!

00:09:46.221 --> 00:09:47.513
I said swear it!

00:09:47.514 --> 00:09:50.432
Very well. I swear it.

00:09:50.433 --> 00:09:52.142
But the amount of electricity...

00:09:52.143 --> 00:09:55.980
Why, we'd basically need our
own hydroelectric generator.

00:09:55.981 --> 00:09:58.232
I really don't think
there's any possible...

00:09:59.943 --> 00:10:01.652
Eureka!

00:10:01.653 --> 00:10:05.572
As you all know, I do my
best thinking on the toilet.

00:10:05.573 --> 00:10:07.992
We know! Stop telling us!

00:10:07.993 --> 00:10:09.827
I didn't even have to go.

00:10:09.828 --> 00:10:13.789
I was just sitting here,
wiling away a Sunday afternoon,

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:15.749
when suddenly, it hit me!

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:18.252
A new source of electricity!

00:10:18.253 --> 00:10:21.547
Would you care to tell us
about it... in another room?

00:10:21.548 --> 00:10:23.173
No!

00:10:23.174 --> 00:10:25.175
According to these old maps,

00:10:25.176 --> 00:10:27.595
which I use in lieu
of toilet paper...

00:10:27.596 --> 00:10:29.263
Ew!

00:10:29.264 --> 00:10:31.223
The main New New York sewer line

00:10:31.224 --> 00:10:34.018
runs directly under
Planet Express.

00:10:41.109 --> 00:10:43.944
We'll simply
drill into the pipe,

00:10:43.945 --> 00:10:46.196
drop this turbine
into the torrent,

00:10:46.197 --> 00:10:49.366
and voila! Free clean power!

00:10:49.367 --> 00:10:52.202
- Clean?
- Oh my, no.

00:10:56.166 --> 00:10:58.667
We're approaching
the main pipeline.

00:10:58.668 --> 00:11:02.588
Can you imagine the quantity of
sewage running through there?

00:11:02.589 --> 00:11:03.798
Yes!

00:11:07.385 --> 00:11:10.220
Contact in four! Three!

00:11:10.221 --> 00:11:12.097
Number two!

00:11:21.358 --> 00:11:23.317
Let's rarely speak
of that again.

00:11:23.318 --> 00:11:27.154
This should generate enough power
to keep the simulation running.

00:11:27.155 --> 00:11:29.990
And it's substantially
higher resolution!

00:11:33.286 --> 00:11:35.622
Let's see how my guys are doing.

00:11:37.248 --> 00:11:38.916
Good news, everyone!

00:11:38.917 --> 00:11:42.044
We have a delivery
to the King of Space.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:48.092
Aw, they're so cute!

00:11:48.093 --> 00:11:49.677
Now I care about them!

00:11:49.678 --> 00:11:52.972
Happy, Bender? We saved
your little friends.

00:11:52.973 --> 00:11:54.473
I sure did.

00:11:54.474 --> 00:11:58.310
In other news,
I've made a huge breakthrough!

00:11:58.311 --> 00:12:00.854
- What is it, Professor?
- No, him.

00:12:00.855 --> 00:12:04.275
- What is it, Professor?
- After many sleepless nights

00:12:04.276 --> 00:12:07.861
and an equal number of
glorious sleep-filled days,

00:12:07.862 --> 00:12:11.198
I've completed my
greatest achievement!

00:12:12.617 --> 00:12:16.288
A simulation of our
entire universe!

00:12:18.164 --> 00:12:19.790
Good news, everyone!

00:12:19.791 --> 00:12:22.793
We have a delivery
to Space Italy!

00:12:33.763 --> 00:12:36.473
Sweet facsimile of Space Italy!

00:12:36.474 --> 00:12:38.100
A simulation...

00:12:38.101 --> 00:12:40.019
Within a simulation!?

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:42.605
Where does it all end?
- Hopefully there.

00:12:42.606 --> 00:12:44.648
Already my head hurts.

00:12:44.649 --> 00:12:48.235
Professor, if you can make
a whole simulated universe,

00:12:48.236 --> 00:12:50.529
isn't it possible
that our own universe

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.448
is also a simulation?

00:12:52.449 --> 00:12:54.116
Absolutely not!

00:12:54.117 --> 00:12:56.827
You sound like a
stoned freshman!

00:12:56.828 --> 00:13:00.414
I mean, what if our laws of
physics are just the computer code

00:13:00.415 --> 00:13:03.959
of some big brilliant
professor playing god up there?

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:05.628
Nailed it!

00:13:05.629 --> 00:13:09.131
Hm. Quantum mechanics
is pretty ridiculous,

00:13:09.132 --> 00:13:10.758
but it's a moot point.

00:13:10.759 --> 00:13:12.968
Even if we are living
in a simulation,

00:13:12.969 --> 00:13:15.846
there's no possible
way of knowing.

00:13:17.182 --> 00:13:18.474
Yes?

00:13:18.475 --> 00:13:20.726
Oh, nothing. I just had
a loogie in my throat.

00:13:20.727 --> 00:13:23.187
Possibly a simulated
loogie.

00:13:23.188 --> 00:13:26.357
What's that? A
g-g-g-grid overload?

00:13:26.358 --> 00:13:30.069
My simulation is drawing a
lot of power for some reason.

00:13:31.821 --> 00:13:35.783
Ah! It appears two black
holes just collided in there.

00:13:35.784 --> 00:13:39.620
Can you imagine how complex
that computation is?

00:13:39.621 --> 00:13:42.498
The Simputron is really
straining to keep up.

00:13:45.418 --> 00:13:47.252
Oh, my glorsh!

00:13:47.253 --> 00:13:50.631
Maybe there is a way to find
out if we live in a simulation.

00:13:50.632 --> 00:13:51.840
Well, I doubt that.

00:13:51.841 --> 00:13:53.592
Double doubt it!

00:13:53.593 --> 00:13:55.803
If our universe is a simulation,

00:13:55.804 --> 00:13:58.430
then it's running on some
kind of computer, right?

00:13:58.431 --> 00:13:59.807
I'm with you so far.

00:13:59.808 --> 00:14:02.393
Actually, I'm not. Is
this about a new soda?

00:14:02.394 --> 00:14:05.604
Suppose we made something
happen that was impossible

00:14:05.605 --> 00:14:08.357
for that big
computer to simulate.

00:14:08.358 --> 00:14:10.276
It would overload!

00:14:10.277 --> 00:14:11.735
Exactly!

00:14:11.736 --> 00:14:13.320
Cool! And then what?

00:14:13.321 --> 00:14:17.032
I don't know! Probably stuff
would pixelate and look weird!

00:14:17.033 --> 00:14:19.535
The laws of physics would fail!

00:14:19.536 --> 00:14:23.122
Like playing a new video game on
a crummy underpowered game system!

00:14:23.123 --> 00:14:24.373
Precisely!

00:14:24.374 --> 00:14:26.793
That my cheapskate
grandma got me.

00:14:27.794 --> 00:14:30.838
Some phenomena are
so wildly complex

00:14:30.839 --> 00:14:34.466
that they'd be impossible
for any computer to simulate.

00:14:34.467 --> 00:14:37.553
For example, a
collapsing magnetic star

00:14:37.554 --> 00:14:39.138
or magnetar.

00:14:39.139 --> 00:14:42.850
But such an event might not
happen for millions of years.

00:14:42.851 --> 00:14:46.729
But, what if we intentionally
caused a magnetar to collapse?

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:50.357
Then, we could just watch and
see if the universe glitches out.

00:14:50.358 --> 00:14:53.193
Of course! And we'd
know once and for all

00:14:53.194 --> 00:14:55.195
if we're living in a simulation.

00:14:57.782 --> 00:15:01.452
Although, I'm not sure I
wanna know the answer to that.

00:15:01.453 --> 00:15:04.246
Me neither. I like resting
secure in the knowledge

00:15:04.247 --> 00:15:05.706
that I'm the real deal.

00:15:05.707 --> 00:15:08.834
Guess
again, loser.

00:15:11.379 --> 00:15:13.047
Let's put it to a vote.

00:15:13.048 --> 00:15:16.342
Who here wants to test if
we're living in a simulation?

00:15:17.636 --> 00:15:21.013
And who would rather continue
living in shameful ignorance?

00:15:21.014 --> 00:15:22.765
That one!

00:15:22.766 --> 00:15:25.309
You all voted for two things.

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:28.854
Honestly. I wanna know if I'm
not living in a simulation,

00:15:28.855 --> 00:15:30.189
but not if I am.

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:31.440
Does that make sense?

00:15:31.441 --> 00:15:34.945
Surprisingly, yes. Let's
just forget about it.

00:15:35.904 --> 00:15:38.113
Although, now we're
always gonna be wondering.

00:15:38.114 --> 00:15:39.448
Let's just go.

00:15:44.537 --> 00:15:45.996
Uh-oh. Not good.

00:15:45.997 --> 00:15:47.915
Not good at all.

00:15:47.916 --> 00:15:51.502
My half-baked software
absolutely will not be able

00:15:51.503 --> 00:15:54.088
to simulate a
collapsing magnetar.

00:15:54.089 --> 00:15:56.215
Oh, I never should
have outsourced it

00:15:56.216 --> 00:15:58.384
to that Indian middle schooler.

00:15:58.385 --> 00:16:01.804
But, the simulations will
find out they're simulations!

00:16:01.805 --> 00:16:05.474
You swore a strip club oath
that would never happen.

00:16:05.475 --> 00:16:07.977
Alas, there'll be
no hiding the truth

00:16:07.978 --> 00:16:10.521
when they see that
magnetar glitching out

00:16:10.522 --> 00:16:14.024
like a big flaming
ball of Microsoft Word.

00:16:14.025 --> 00:16:17.444
Well, if they're
gonna find out anyway,

00:16:17.445 --> 00:16:19.446
I should be the
one to tell them.

00:16:19.447 --> 00:16:22.366
I'm the only one who
truly understands!

00:16:22.367 --> 00:16:24.493
Plus, I like
delivering bad news.

00:16:24.494 --> 00:16:27.288
Actually, that
might be possible.

00:16:27.289 --> 00:16:29.415
Since you're basically
just software

00:16:29.416 --> 00:16:31.875
in a greasy wad of
aluminum foil...

00:16:31.876 --> 00:16:32.876
Aw...

00:16:32.877 --> 00:16:35.671
I could extract your
programming, compress it,

00:16:35.672 --> 00:16:38.465
and inject it into
Simulated Bender.

00:16:38.466 --> 00:16:41.719
You'd take his place
in the simulated world.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:43.345
But what would happen to him?

00:16:43.346 --> 00:16:46.307
He'd be pushed through
to the sub-simulation.

00:16:46.308 --> 00:16:47.516
And that Bender?

00:16:47.517 --> 00:16:50.477
It's Benders all the way down.

00:16:50.478 --> 00:16:52.563
Alright. I'm going in.

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:55.566
I must warn you, Bender.

00:16:55.567 --> 00:16:57.568
It'll be a one-way trip.

00:16:57.569 --> 00:16:59.945
There's no way of returning.

00:16:59.946 --> 00:17:02.239
That's okay. I don't
wanna live in a world

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:04.617
where I'm less real
than everyone else.

00:17:04.618 --> 00:17:06.327
Those are my people in there,

00:17:06.328 --> 00:17:07.828
in Baloney Town.

00:17:10.498 --> 00:17:12.958
Ooh!

00:17:12.959 --> 00:17:15.294
In a few minutes,
you should reboot

00:17:15.295 --> 00:17:19.131
in the simulated world
as Simulated Bender.

00:17:19.132 --> 00:17:20.466
Or you might die.

00:17:20.467 --> 00:17:24.386
Goodbye,
precious friends and coworkers.

00:17:24.387 --> 00:17:27.765
Goodbye, sewage-stained
floor tiles.

00:17:27.766 --> 00:17:28.974
Goodbye, Zoidberg.

00:17:28.975 --> 00:17:31.769
How will I go on without you?

00:17:38.109 --> 00:17:39.945
I'll get a broom.

00:17:48.495 --> 00:17:51.163
Holding outside magnetar
implosion range.

00:17:51.164 --> 00:17:53.123
We'll be safe at this distance,

00:17:53.124 --> 00:17:56.001
even if, God forbid, we're real.

00:17:56.002 --> 00:17:58.712
Then it's time to put
reality to the test.

00:17:58.713 --> 00:18:01.048
- I'm scared!
- I am, too.

00:18:01.049 --> 00:18:03.676
But it's actually
kind of beautiful.

00:18:03.677 --> 00:18:06.387
Would it be any less
beautiful if it weren't real?

00:18:06.388 --> 00:18:07.888
And we weren't real?

00:18:07.889 --> 00:18:09.974
We'll find out soon enough.

00:18:09.975 --> 00:18:12.852
Begin monopole bombardment!

00:18:25.573 --> 00:18:27.992
You okay, buddy?

00:18:27.993 --> 00:18:30.119
No!

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:31.829
Probably a bad clam.

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:33.747
I think I'm gonna reboot!

00:18:33.748 --> 00:18:34.749
Oh...

00:18:37.794 --> 00:18:39.503
Where... Where am I?

00:18:39.504 --> 00:18:40.921
You're right here, Bender.

00:18:40.922 --> 00:18:43.716
Just outside magnetar
implosion range.

00:18:43.717 --> 00:18:45.884
Oh... Right.

00:18:45.885 --> 00:18:47.177
Baloney Town.

00:18:48.471 --> 00:18:50.764
Guys? I have
something to tell you,

00:18:50.765 --> 00:18:52.683
and it'll be the
hardest bad news

00:18:52.684 --> 00:18:54.893
I've ever had the
pleasure of delivering.

00:18:54.894 --> 00:18:57.104
Shush, Bender! We're
about to find out

00:18:57.105 --> 00:18:59.023
if we're living in a simulation!

00:18:59.024 --> 00:19:01.817
Right... It-it's
about that. See...

00:19:01.818 --> 00:19:04.320
I've been thinking about
that, too, actually.

00:19:04.321 --> 00:19:05.821
And you wanna know what I think?

00:19:05.822 --> 00:19:09.618
- Do I!
- I think it makes no difference at all.

00:19:10.035 --> 00:19:13.537
Either way, the laws of the
universe are way beyond our control.

00:19:13.538 --> 00:19:15.289
So, what can we do?

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:17.167
We just make the best of it.

00:19:17.584 --> 00:19:20.753
I don't know what we're about
to see, Leela, but I love you.

00:19:20.754 --> 00:19:22.671
Now and forever.

00:19:22.672 --> 00:19:24.381
And that much is real,

00:19:24.382 --> 00:19:26.258
even if we're not.

00:19:27.928 --> 00:19:30.262
Hm... The dummy's right.

00:19:30.263 --> 00:19:32.431
I feel, therefore I am.

00:19:32.432 --> 00:19:34.683
It doesn't matter if I'm real?

00:19:34.684 --> 00:19:36.435
Not one bit.

00:19:36.436 --> 00:19:38.520
So what did you
wanna tell us, robot?

00:19:38.521 --> 00:19:41.523
Just... thank you!

00:19:44.110 --> 00:19:46.487
That's robots for you.

00:19:46.488 --> 00:19:49.239
Now, let's sit back
and enjoy the show.

00:19:54.329 --> 00:19:57.831
Oh, lordy-loo. The
magnetar is about to pop!

00:19:57.832 --> 00:19:59.875
How's the Simputron holding up?

00:19:59.876 --> 00:20:02.127
Processor overload!

00:20:02.128 --> 00:20:04.213
The cooling fan's on fire!

00:20:04.214 --> 00:20:05.339
Whoa!

00:20:10.553 --> 00:20:13.264
Pull the plug! Stop the simulation!

00:20:13.265 --> 00:20:15.099
No! Bender's in there!

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:18.102
There's no choice. This building's
about to go up in smoke,

00:20:18.103 --> 00:20:21.982
and I've got doomsday devices
hidden in every nook and cranny.

00:20:23.942 --> 00:20:25.484
I'm sorry, buddy.

00:20:25.485 --> 00:20:28.487
I know you can't hear me,
but we tried our best.

00:20:28.488 --> 00:20:30.531
At least you got to
go out with dignity.

00:20:34.786 --> 00:20:36.746
Rebooting.

00:20:37.831 --> 00:20:39.748
Where... Where am I?

00:20:39.749 --> 00:20:41.709
Right here, in the universe.

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:45.254
Oh... I had to come
tell you something...

00:20:45.255 --> 00:20:49.091
Bender? How did you possibly
manage to come back?

00:20:49.092 --> 00:20:52.219
Don't be rude, Professor,
Bender was speaking first.

00:20:52.220 --> 00:20:53.929
What did you wanna
tell us, robot?

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:55.389
It's just that...

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:57.766
I know how to save
the simulation.

00:20:57.767 --> 00:21:00.311
Oh, please. There's
no possible...

00:21:01.855 --> 00:21:03.565
Eureka!

00:21:05.567 --> 00:21:08.360
I made the change you
suggested, Bender.

00:21:08.361 --> 00:21:11.781
Although it took a lot of
toilet time to fully comprehend.

00:21:12.782 --> 00:21:15.034
We won't need
nearly so much power

00:21:15.035 --> 00:21:17.745
now that I've under-clocked
the processor.

00:21:17.746 --> 00:21:20.331
But, won't the
simulation run slower?

00:21:20.332 --> 00:21:22.207
Oh, much slower.

00:21:22.208 --> 00:21:25.836
Are we talking regular
slow or bureaucrat slow?

00:21:25.837 --> 00:21:27.630
Infinitely slower than that.

00:21:29.049 --> 00:21:31.467
So they'll be in, like, a coma?

00:21:31.468 --> 00:21:32.885
Oh my, no!

00:21:32.886 --> 00:21:35.095
They'll never notice
any difference.

00:21:35.096 --> 00:21:38.057
But while they live out
one second of their lives,

00:21:38.058 --> 00:21:41.226
years, if not centuries,
will pass for us.

00:21:41.227 --> 00:21:44.313
Aw, then I guess we won't
get to spy on them anymore.

00:21:44.314 --> 00:21:45.856
Spy all you like.

00:21:45.857 --> 00:21:49.401
But it's about to get
very, very boring.

00:21:49.402 --> 00:21:50.903
Not for them.

00:22:07.462 --> 00:22:09.463
Pixels...

00:22:11.466 --> 00:22:15.177
To make it real, really real

00:22:15.178 --> 00:22:16.972
She says

00:22:17.555 --> 00:22:20.849
You just have to be here

00:22:20.850 --> 00:22:22.851
rock guitar riff

00:22:22.852 --> 00:22:26.397
On this satellite

00:22:26.398 --> 00:22:28.565
Satellite

00:22:28.566 --> 00:22:30.860
Had to be here

00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:36.031
On this satellite

00:22:36.032 --> 00:22:38.158
Satellite

00:22:38.159 --> 00:22:40.161
Had to be here

00:22:42.038 --> 00:22:44.708
On this satellite

00:22:47.794 --> 00:22:50.171
Had to be here

00:22:51.715 --> 00:22:54.718
On this satellite

00:23:00.682 --> 00:23:03.684
Song slowly fades

00:23:03.685 --> 00:23:07.187
electronic distortion

00:23:07.188 --> 00:23:10.191
soft, orchestral
music playing